# 📐 Decision Boundary

One of the most important concepts behind the perceptron is the **decision boundary**.

For two-dimensional data, the perceptron creates a line:

```text
w₁x₁ + w₂x₂ + b = 0
```

This line separates two classes.

```text
        Class 1
      ●  ●  ●
    ●  ●  ●
--------------------  ← Decision Boundary
      ○  ○  ○
    ○  ○  ○
        Class 2
```

For higher-dimensional data, this becomes a **hyperplane**.

